  "worked_solution": "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in {-1,0,1,2},\\,y\\in {-2,-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
